## Manhunt and capture

After the photos were released, the suspects allegedly shot Sean Collier of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology Police Department multiple times, killing him. The brothers were motivated by their "extremist Islamic beliefs" but "were not connected to any known terrorist groups". According to The Los Angeles Times, a law enforcement official said Dzhokhar "did not seem as bothered about America's role in the Muslim world" as his brother Tamerlan had been worried. Dzhokhar identified his brother as the mastermind or "driving force" behind the bombings and said Tamerlan had only recently recruited him to help. New York Police Commissioner Raymond Kelly said that Dzhokhar had told investigators that the brothers "decided spontaneously" to go to New York after they carjacked an SUV and that they planned to bomb Times Square.

